        <td>16 Deck Skills, Portal Website (dist), GitHub Pages Deployment, LLM Testing Protocol</td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h1>1. Overview & Objective</h1>
<p>This document details the exact procedures for uploading the Lintas Presentation Design System codebase to a corporate GitHub repository, enabling instant live hosting via <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>, and guiding personnel across all eight departments to download, install, and test their assigned presentation skills in their bespoke LLMs (Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, Antigravity, Copilot, and Cursor).</p>

<div class="callout">
    <strong>📌 Key Benefit for Lintas Personnel:</strong> By enabling GitHub Pages, team members do <em>not</em> need to install Git, Python, or node.js. They simply open the live URL in any web browser, select their department and role, download their pre-packaged skill, and follow the 2-minute setup guide for their bespoke LLM.
</div>

<h1>2. Repository Structure & Files to Upload</h1>
<p>Ensure your local workspace directory contains the following verified components before pushing:</p>

<table>
    <tr>
        <th style="width:30%;">Directory / File</th>
        <th style="width:30%;">Purpose</th>
        <th style="width:40%;">Includes</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Lintas_Group_16_Lintas_Deck_Skills/</strong></td>
        <td>Source repository for all 16 skills</td>
        <td>16 folders, each with <span class="tag">SKILL.md</span>, <span class="tag">assets/brand/</span>, <span class="tag">assets/textures/</span>, and <span class="tag">assets/uploads/</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #FAF8F3;">
        <td><strong>portal/</strong></td>
        <td>Skill download website project</td>
        <td><span class="tag">build_portal.py</span>, <span class="tag">roles.json</span>, <span class="tag">start_portal.bat</span>, <span class="tag">README.md</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>portal/dist/</strong></td>
        <td>Static site for GitHub Pages</td>
        <td><span class="tag">index.html</span>, <span class="tag">styles.css</span>, <span class="tag">app.js</span>, <span class="tag">skills-manifest.json</span>, <span class="tag">checksums.txt</span>, and 48 packages in <span class="tag">downloads/</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #FAF8F3;">
        <td><strong>lintas-deck-skill-portal/</strong></td>
        <td>Architecture specification</td>
        <td><span class="tag">SKILL.md</span> defining portal capabilities and deployment rules</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Lintas Presentation Design System.pptx</strong></td>
        <td>Visual reference presentation</td>
        <td>Original native shape deck (69 KB)</td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h1>3. Step-by-Step GitHub Upload Instructions</h1>
<p>Execute the following commands in PowerShell from the project root folder:</p>

<h2>Step 3.1: Navigate to Workspace Root</h2>
<div class="code-block">cd "D:\VIBE Coding (2026)\Lintas Presentation Design System"</div>

<h2>Step 3.2: Verify .gitignore Configuration</h2>
<p>Ensure that temporary scratch logs or Python cache files are ignored, while keeping <span class="tag">portal/dist</span> and all download archives intact:</p>
<div class="code-block"># Create or verify .gitignore
@"
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.gemini/
scratch/
"@ | Out-File -FilePath .gitignore -Encoding utf8</div>

<h2>Step 3.3: Initialize Git and Create Initial Commit</h2>
<div class="code-block">git init
git add .
git commit -m "feat: initial release of Lintas Deck Skills and Portal Website"</div>

<h2>Step 3.4: Link to GitHub and Push</h2>
<p>Create a new repository on GitHub (e.g. named <strong>lintas-presentation-design-system</strong> in your Lintas Group GitHub organization or user account). Then link and push:</p>
<div class="code-block">git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/&lt;your-org-or-username&gt;/lintas-presentation-design-system.git
git push -u origin main</div>

<h1>4. Enabling Zero-Install Live Access via GitHub Pages</h1>
<p>To allow team members to test and download skills without running any command-line tools:</p>

<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Go to your repository on GitHub.com and click the <strong>Settings</strong> tab.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> In the left navigation menu, click <strong>Pages</strong> under the "Code and automation" heading.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Under "Build and deployment":</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Source:</strong> Deploy from a branch</li>
    <li><strong>Branch:</strong> <span class="tag">main</span></li>
    <li><strong>Folder:</strong> Select <span class="tag">/docs</span> (or <span class="tag">/portal/dist</span> if configured via GitHub Actions)</li>
</ul>

<div class="callout-blue">
    <strong>💡 Tip — Quickest GitHub Pages Setup with /docs Folder:</strong><br>
    GitHub Pages natively supports the <span class="tag">/docs</span> folder on the main branch. Simply copy <span class="tag">portal/dist</span> to <span class="tag">docs/</span> by running:<br>
    <span class="tag">Copy-Item -Recurse -Force portal\dist docs</span><br>
    Then commit and push. In GitHub Pages Settings, choose branch 'main' and folder '/docs'.
</div>

<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Click <strong>Save</strong>. Within 60 seconds, GitHub Pages will deploy your site to:</p>
<div class="code-block">https://&lt;your-org-or-username&gt;.github.io/lintas-presentation-design-system/</div>
<p>Share this URL directly with Lintas Group team members for immediate testing!</p>

<h1>5. Testing Protocol for Lintas Personnel</h1>
<p>Distribute these instructions to designated testers across all 8 departments:</p>

<h2>Phase 1: Selecting Department & Role</h2>
<p>1. Open the portal URL in your web browser (Edge, Chrome, or Firefox).<br>
2. In the top selector bar, pick your <strong>Department</strong> (Business Development, Contract, CTS, Finance, HR/GA, PMO, Procurement, Sales & Marketing).<br>
3. Select your <strong>Role / Focus</strong> (e.g. 'Executive / Strategic' or 'Operations / Specialist').<br>
4. Review the Recommendation Banner. It highlights your recommended skill with a gold badge:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Executive Editorial (-1):</strong> Optimized for executive narrative, board meetings, and high-level decision makers.</li>
    <li><strong>Operational Decision Intelligence (-2):</strong> Engineered for working sprint reviews, SLA metrics, and operational dashboards.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Phase 2: Downloading the Skill Package</h2>
<p>Click one of the three download buttons on your department card:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Download Skill Package (.ZIP):</strong> Complete bundle containing <span class="tag">SKILL.md</span> + <span class="tag">assets/</span> (for Claude, Antigravity, Claude Code).</li>
    <li><strong>System Prompt (.MD):</strong> Standalone markdown instructions (for ChatGPT Custom GPTs, Gemini Gems, or Copilot).</li>
    <li><strong>Assets Pack (.ZIP):</strong> Isolated corporate logos and textures.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Phase 3: Installing into Your Bespoke LLM</h2>
<table>
    <tr>
        <th style="width:25%;">Platform</th>
        <th style="width:20%;">File to Use</th>
        <th style="width:55%;">Setup Action</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Claude (Web & Desktop)</strong></td>
        <td>.ZIP package</td>
        <td>Settings → Capabilities → Skills → Upload ZIP file</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #FAF8F3;">
        <td><strong>Claude Code (CLI / SDK)</strong></td>
        <td>.ZIP package</td>
        <td>Unzip into <span class="tag">~/.claude/skills/</span> or project root <span class="tag">.claude/skills/</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Google Antigravity</strong></td>
        <td>.ZIP package</td>
        <td>Unpack into workspace or <span class="tag">~/.gemini/antigravity/skills/</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #FAF8F3;">
        <td><strong>OpenAI ChatGPT</strong></td>
        <td>.MD file + Assets</td>
        <td>Paste .md into Custom GPT Instructions, upload assets to Knowledge, enable Code Interpreter</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Google Gemini (Gems)</strong></td>
        <td>.MD file + Assets</td>
        <td>Create Gem, paste .md into Instructions, attach logo images</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #FAF8F3;">
        <td><strong>Microsoft Copilot / 365</strong></td>
        <td>.MD file</td>
        <td>Paste .md into Copilot Studio Custom Instructions, link assets in SharePoint</td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2>Phase 4: Run the Standardized Verification Prompt</h2>
<p>To confirm that your bespoke LLM is strictly enforcing the Lintas Presentation Design System, start a new chat session and copy/paste this verification prompt:</p>
<div class="code-block">Use the lintas-deck skill to prepare a 3-slide executive presentation for Lintas Group.
Include:
1. Cover slide with official Lintas Group logo and our department primary and accent colors.
2. Content slide featuring our signature departmental visualization.
3. Closing slide displaying the Menara MTH 16th floor corporate headquarters address block.</div>

<h2>Phase 5: Quality Checklist for Testers</h2>
<div class="checklist-item">☑ <strong>Widescreen Ratio:</strong> Is the deck 16:9 widescreen (13.333 x 7.5 in) with consistent margins (0.55-0.75 in)?</div>
<div class="checklist-item">☑ <strong>Department Palette:</strong> Does it use the exact HEX codes for your department (e.g. Finance: #17263B Navy & #B79A61 Gold)?</div>
<div class="checklist-item">☑ <strong>Typography Restraint:</strong> Are headers Aptos/Calibri (30-42 pt) and labels Consolas (10-13 pt)? No full monospaced paragraphs.</div>
<div class="checklist-item">☑ <strong>Corporate Brand Logo:</strong> Is lintas-group-logo.png placed with clear-space equal to the height of letter 'L'? No distortion.</div>
<div class="checklist-item">☑ <strong>Closing Slide:</strong> Does the final slide include Menara MTH 16th floor, Jl. MT. Haryono kav. 23, and sales@LT-indonesia.com?</div>
<div class="checklist-item">☑ <strong>Brand Neutrality:</strong> Are third-party partner logos excluded unless uploaded dynamically for specific multi-vendor scopes?</div>
<div class="checklist-item">☑ <strong>Editable Shapes:</strong> Are diagrams native PowerPoint shapes/tables rather than flattened AI images?</div>

<h1>6. Feedback & Issue Reporting</h1>
<p>Testers encountering any formatting issues, broken links, or palette anomalies should submit an Issue on the GitHub repository:</p>
<p>1. Navigate to: <span class="tag">https://github.com/&lt;your-org-or-username&gt;/lintas-presentation-design-system/issues</span><br>
2. Click 'New Issue' and include:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Department & Role tested (e.g. PMO / Delivery Lead)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• LLM Platform tested (e.g. Claude Desktop 3.7 Sonnet, ChatGPT Plus, Gemini Gem)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Attached screenshot or generated .pptx slide<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Description of unexpected visual behavior</p>

